  "reason": "The best result so far is config_041 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted + multiprofile) at 0.725. All four aggregation×fusion combinations for that exact encoder pair have been tested. The strongest untested direction is to keep the proven best components (scvi_n200, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion, multiprofile) while substituting resnet50 for imagenet_vit_l (config_022). Evidence shows resnet50 trails imagenet_vit_l by ~0.028 with avgpool+weighted (0.678 vs 0.706), but the transformer aggregation added ~0.019 on top of avgpool with imagenet_vit_l, so config_022 is expected around 0.69–0.71. Among all untested configurations, this has the highest expected accuracy because it retains the three strongest factors (RNA encoder, aggregation, fusion) and only changes the image backbone. As the final experiment, this maximizes the probability of either confirming the robustness of the transformer+weighted design or discovering a marginally better result, while all other untested options (scgpt, pca_n2000, singleprofile, rna_only, image_only) are strongly indicated by prior evidence to underperform."
}

